## solutions

#### using a hashmap (unordered_map)

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <unordered_map>

char mostFrequentChar(std::string s) {
  std::unordered_map<char, int> count;
  for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i += 1) {
    count[s[i]] += 1;
  }

  char best = '\0';
  for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i += 1) {
    char current = s[i];
    if (best == '\0' || count[current] > count[best]) {
      best = current;
    }
  }
  return best;
}
```

- n = length of string
- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(n)
